{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/19685-have-you-ever-used-googles-maps-engine-for-your-territories","id":19685,"title":"Have you ever used googles \"maps engine\" for your territories?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-28T06:14:52-08:00","id":19685,"title":"Have you ever used googles \"maps engine\" for your territories?","content":"Obligitory Hello I am new to the forums!<br /> <br /> I have been playing WoD for a while now over all of the splats and in an ongoing cross splat game and my GM from that introduced me to the idea of using googles Map Engine to lay out features in his world.<br /> <br /> I am currently GMing my second werewolf game and instead of writing my world down into a large book (full of pasted pictures of maps) I instead am using googles Map Engine.<br /> So far I have found it really incredible for laying out territories for my local packs, setting up landmarks for potential story hooks, placing things inside my packs territory and so fourth.<br /> <br /> I have on map called &quot;The GM Map&quot;<br /> and another map called &quot;The player Map&quot;<br /> Boy am I original with my titles.<br /> <br /> However as my players discover new things in the world I simply add a marker to the player map and write a little about it. The players can also add their own markers and regularly update many of the features in their territory. It makes it much more collaborative than the usual &quot;GM book&quot; system and the players often add things in between sessions.. I get a few texts a week asking if they can do research rolls in between sessions on this or that to get more information on the map.<br /> <br /> I guess what I am wondering is has anyone used this tech before and if so do you have any advice for me?<br /> <br /> Also sorry if this is in the wrong place just figured since I am doing it for territories id post it in werewolf!<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Thought I would add a link to my work in progress for a new map that I started making yesterday<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://mapsengine.google.com/map/edit?mid=z4QcyiNPoaNw.kftNnoT2F20o\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.google.com/maps/d/thumbnail?mid=1dBcCu0b5JyOm1g1emgsLcAxutZ8\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mapsengine.google.com/map/edit?mid=z4QcyiNPoaNw.kftNnoT2F20o\" target=\"_blank\"> Sanguine my brother - Google My Maps </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mapsengine.google.com/map/edit?mid=z4QcyiNPoaNw.kftNnoT2F20o\" target=\"_blank\"> https://mapsengine.google.com/map/edit?mid=z4QcyiNPoaNw.kftNnoT2F20o </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Sanguine my brother </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1387-moxy","user":"Moxy","date":". 11-28-2013, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1387-moxy","name":"Moxy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1387_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T15:43:19-08:00","id":21328,"title":"","content":"I've thought about doing it but my werewolf game fell through. It is a neat idea, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T08:57:51-08:00","id":25142,"title":"","content":"This is the link to map of Paris:<br /> <br /> (player's map)<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://mapsengine.google.com/map/viewer?mid=z0Utsy8qtCss.kH2OdP4wGRGQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.google.com/maps/d/thumbnail?mid=1yK_fEp1rEH3BfBiDkDJyy_xwIfs\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mapsengine.google.com/map/viewer?mid=z0Utsy8qtCss.kH2OdP4wGRGQ\" target=\"_blank\"> WtF - ObiWanKennedy - Google My Maps </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mapsengine.google.com/map/viewer?mid=z0Utsy8qtCss.kH2OdP4wGRGQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://mapsengine.google.com/map/viewer?mid=z0Utsy8qtCss.kH2OdP4wGRGQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Loup-Garou : Les d&eacute;chus MJ : ObiWanKennedy </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The ST map is not public. I can share with you if you want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1549-obiwankennedy","name":"ObiWanKennedy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T17:05:54-08:00","id":25434,"title":"","content":"Wow...thanks for bringing this up. My group is about to launch into a very large campaign where the city, New York, is the focal point and we're each going to play and run most of the splats, and how each group interacts and effects each other through their actions in the city. I was divvying up the territories and I see this thread and you've made my life easier now. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T07:19:40-08:00","id":33159,"title":"","content":"I really like that map of Paris that you have there, the picture embedding is a really neat idea, i just need to learn a bit more french :P<br /> <br /> At Troller.<br /> Your very welcome, My current cross splat GM uses it to great effect, it is very helpful for tracking things like nomadic movements of werewolves. He also has large areas sectioned off for the courts.<br /> <br /> I think it makes keeping track all that much easier.<br /> <br /> <br /> Perhaps this thread should get moved somewhere else, so that it can be seen by more people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1387-moxy","name":"Moxy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1387_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T12:11:09-08:00","id":41233,"title":"","content":"Hey Guys,<br /> <br /> Moxy, I have used the map in the past but only for my own GM tracking. I actually did a post about it on my silly little table top blog here <a href=\"http://wp.me/p3JqWf-gi\" target=\"_blank\">http://wp.me/p3JqWf-gi</a> . It really helped me keep organized. I am starting a new campaign in two weeks that is essentially a Werewolf version of Supernatural which I created a map, this time much bigger, of locations and actions.<br /> <br /> I have not ever shared one with the players and love that idea. I think I will have to make a second one however as I do not want them to see all the notes I have. I would love to see an update on how your game is progressing using the maps!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1883,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1883-face_plont","user":"Face_Plont","date":". 01-02-2014, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1883-face_plont","name":"Face_Plont","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1883_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T22:53:42-08:00","id":43970,"title":"","content":"That is awesome but it leads me to ask a question. Is there a program that would allow me to build a realistic map of a city that doesn't actually exist? when I came to this thread that's what I thought it was. The Paris one was awesome too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T09:29:32-08:00","id":44234,"title":"","content":"I have not found a good free source for online fantasy maps. Google Maps Pro and ESRI both provide pay to use editors and publishers. I like ESRI for its modular map usage (and its ability to create/use ANY map fictional or real), and editors of base map data sets, Google Map Pro is slick, but is best for Google supported map sets (earth and Mars now).<br /> <br /> Alternately I have tried Fantasy Cartographer. Its actually easier to fashion a map with it, and using a Free ESRI account you can publish player maps. Limitations still apply.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, I end up using GIMP and draw my own maps, I composite historic maps with modern maps. Then I upload them to ESRI and use the mapping tools. It costs $100 for the licensed version. (I also use it for my running blog)<br /> <br /> I do this because I like to add layers of average Gauntlet Strength and Shadow Resonance for the city. Plus I map locus, verge, Aversion gate, Hallows, Trods, Essence flows, and significant territories. Otherwise I create PDFs, and allow my players to annotate the PDF as they need. Neither tool is perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1336-gideon","name":"Gideon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T12:34:56-08:00","id":49979,"title":"","content":"I'm planning to use maps as reference for all of my games going forward but I really like your example ObiWan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T13:55:03-08:00","id":50045,"title":"","content":"I'm going to have to use this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T18:17:56-08:00","id":62635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ObiWanKennedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/19685-have-you-ever-used-googles-maps-engine-for-your-territories?p=25142#post25142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the link to map of Paris:<br /> <br /> (player's map)<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://mapsengine.google.com/map/viewer?mid=z0Utsy8qtCss.kH2OdP4wGRGQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.google.com/maps/d/thumbnail?mid=1yK_fEp1rEH3BfBiDkDJyy_xwIfs\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mapsengine.google.com/map/viewer?mid=z0Utsy8qtCss.kH2OdP4wGRGQ\" target=\"_blank\"> WtF - ObiWanKennedy - Google My Maps </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mapsengine.google.com/map/viewer?mid=z0Utsy8qtCss.kH2OdP4wGRGQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://mapsengine.google.com/map/viewer?mid=z0Utsy8qtCss.kH2OdP4wGRGQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Loup-Garou : Les d&eacute;chus MJ : ObiWanKennedy </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The ST map is not public. I can share with you if you want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love how yours has pictures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T12:05:58-08:00","id":67321,"title":"","content":"Here's mine for my Mayo, Yukon chronicle.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://mapsengine.google.com/map/edit?mid=zcwBdMwjmifM.ky9OlNUDEywc\" target=\"_blank\">https://mapsengine.google.com/map/ed...M.ky9OlNUDEywc</a><br /> <br /> Shows off the territory of the main pack, and several notable locations in town. Some may notice a few things from the free W:tF Demo, which I used as our first story but in my own setting. There are several nearby Uratha as well, though because of the size of the Yukon, the nearest is 35km away, with the farthest pack they know of is nearly 120km. And as you might expect they don't really get along with the closest pack lol.<br /> <br /> The map is constantly used and updated during gameplay (we play over Roll20 do to distance) and you may notice a few Wounds in the town as the story revolves around these wounds forming for unknown reasons atm as well as dealing with a nest of beshilu that has been discovered below the local school.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","user":"Xaielao","date":". 02-07-2014, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}